# Canonical normalized CompiledFrameProgram hash for make_determinism_fixture.
# Regenerate only when the compiled-program contract intentionally changes.
#
# 2026-09-15 — INTENTIONAL contract change, previously 0x610ce49755184814.
# Image layers no longer lower into the fused storage-image batch: every
# reachable image source carries scene-binding metadata, so
# is_fusible_layer_node() excludes all of them and fusion survives only for
# TextRun sources. The normalized program therefore contains the standalone
# image/transform/composite operations and no batch entries.
# The retired value was regenerated on 2026-08-27 for the pre-retirement
# contract; see docs/tickets/TICKET-SCALE-P0-ASSET-VRAM-GOP.md for the evidence
# (including why this changed in 00be928ab without the golden being updated).
#
# 2026-10-08 — regenerated after the PixelProgram CPU fusion and fusion-path
# stabilization commits (159d38775, 46ba63654); previous value 0x65304b41dbf40d8f.
# The new value is stable across repeated runs of the fixture.
#
# 2026-10-20 — regenerated after the static-bake cacheability fix (80119a1b9);
# previous value 0x1ec334584fada888. Composite nodes are now excluded from
# static-bake islands (compute_static_bake_islands keeps them frame-dependent
# per evaluate_cache), so the normalized program carries different K entries.
# The new value is stable across repeated runs; covered by the sibling test
# "static bakes exclude noncacheable composites".
# 2026-10-23 — updated after the render-graph compiler produced a new stable
# normalized program. Two independent compilations match; full node/operation
# parity remains asserted above. Previous golden: 0xaccd5b842ed2c6a2.
#
# 2026-11-12 — INTENTIONAL contract change, previously 0x3b196a95fae3f89e.
# The physical-slot planner now treats composite resources as frame-dependent
# (87c3761b9), so composites are aliasable and receive planned output slots
# instead of being excluded as persistent. The normalized program therefore
# carries new P entries. The fixture's topology and stable-node IDs are
# unchanged: its nodes carry no layer_id, and the compiler pipeline is
# otherwise unchanged since 5229e2605. Reproducible across two independent
# compilations of make_determinism_fixture.
# Evidence: 87c3761b9; "FrameGraphCompiler - compiled frame program is
